\newlabel{fig:trac}{{4}{19}{Two answers to ``will the agent misbehave?''. Left: TRAC observes a single agent's trace at run time, abstracts events to propositions with language-model labelers, checks an LTL constraint, predicts violations by sampling continuations, and intervenes. Right: this paper classifies every branch of a multiparty protocol before any run, deterministically and exactly. Complementary: TRAC's constraints can supply $\Haz $; its monitor can enforce at run time what the condition certified}{figure.caption.27}{}}
\newlabel{fig:trac@cref}{{[figure][4][]4}{[1][19][]19}}
\newlabel{tab:trac}{{4}{19}{Axes on which the two approaches differ}{table.caption.28}{}}
\newlabel{tab:trac@cref}{{[table][4][]4}{[1][19][]19}}
